<title>SWEDEN: TABLE-SANDVIK H1 PROFIT FALLS 18 PCT.</title>
<headline>TABLE-SANDVIK H1 PROFIT FALLS 18 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish speciality tools maker and engineer Sandvik reported on Tuesday for the first six months of 1997.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  2,105 vs  2,555</p>
<p> Invoiced sales			   15,482 vs 14,589</p>
<p> Order intake			     16,158 vs 14,383</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)		10.05*vs  12.60</p>
<p> Cost of goods sold		     10,294 vs  9,316</p>
<p> Production, sale, admin costs	 3,273 vs  3,073</p>
<p> Associate interests			 221 vs     73</p>
<p> Other costs/income	     CHARGE    54 vs     52 CREDIT</p>
<p> Operating profit			  2,082 vs  2,325</p>
<p> Net financial items			  23 vs    230</p>
<p> Tax					     620 vs    709</p>
<p> Minorities				     78 vs     74</p>
<p> Net profit				  1,407 vs  1,772</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuters poll found the market expected a profit after financial items of 2.17 billion crowns for the first half of 1997. *=takes into account share redemption carried out by Sandvik in June this year</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
